---
import { getEntry, render } from "astro:content";
import DocShell from "../../layouts/DocShell.astro";
import { sdkSidebar } from "../../lib/sdk-nav";
import "../../styles/prose.css";

const snippet = await getEntry("snippets", "python-sdk");
const { Content: Example } = await render(snippet!);
---

<DocShell title="SDKs" description="Client libraries for the OpenHAL hub protocol." sidebar={sdkSidebar()} section="SDKs">
  <p>An SDK speaks the hub protocol for you. The hub's safety kernel still decides every command.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Language</th><th scope="col">Package</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><a href="/sdks/python/">Python</a></td>
          <td class="mono">openhal.client</td>
          <td>reference</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><a href="/sdks/typescript/">TypeScript</a></td>
          <td class="mono">not published</td>
          <td><span class="status planned">planned</span></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <h2 id="python">Python</h2>
  <p>The Python SDK ships in the repository. A blocked command comes back as a decision, not an exception.</p>
  <Example />
  <p><a href="/sdks/python/">Python guide</a> and <a href="/sdks/python/reference/">API reference</a></p>
</DocShell>
